                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3fbcff56-5881-33dc-b9ee-f4fad59dc68e",
                        "entry_id": "436698c2-d0a2-3514-bdff-104108aa552f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To undergo recalescence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9efacc55-baae-4d63-9957-4c4e8c041d38",
                                "sense_id": "3fbcff56-5881-33dc-b9ee-f4fad59dc68e",
                                "text": "At Stefan numbers greater than 1, the solidification process cannot recalesce the liquid to its equilibrium point and this is termed hypercooling."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "01390e03-e6a9-4be2-8189-723943734a2d",
                                "sense_id": "3fbcff56-5881-33dc-b9ee-f4fad59dc68e",
                                "text": "One of these has been called recalescence, to which attention was first drawn by Mr. Barrett, who showed that if a piece of hard steel is heated to redness and then allowed to cool slowly it will, when almost black (in a dark room), suddenly reglow or recalesce, and then get dark again."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
